        // In the reference: ok is true, initializedAfter is false
        // In the bug: revert occurs (ok is false), initializedAfter not reached (but we still read it)
        // Actually both conditions must be asserted: the reference holds (true, false), the bug breaks (false, true or false)
        // The correct contract: ok == true && initializedAfter == false
        // The buggy contract: ok == false (because revert) AND initializedAfter remains false since initialized was never set
        // The key divergence is that in reference, availableForFlashLoan does not revert (returns false), in bug it reverts.
        // So assert that ok is true (reference passes) and that initializedAfter is false.
        assertTrue(ok == true && initializedAfter == false);
    }
}

